quran[28]{c,v,t}:
  74,48,"So (now), the intercession of the intercessors will not benefit them."
  74,49,"What is the matter with these (disbelievers) that they (still) turn away from the Reminder,"
  74,50,"as if they were frightened donkeys,"
  74,51,fleeing from a lion?
  74,52,"Rather, each one of them desires to be given unrolled scriptures (for them to read)."
  74,53,"No, indeed! Instead, they do not fear the Hereafter."
  74,54,"No, indeed! This (Qur’an) is a Reminder."
  74,55,So let anyone who wishes remember it.
  74,56,And they will not remember (it) unless Allah wills. He is worthy of (your) being conscious (of Him) and worthy of (granting) forgiveness.
  75,1,I swear by the Day of Resurrection!
  75,2,And I swear by the self-blaming soul!
  75,3,Does human being think We shall not reassemble his bones?
  75,4,"Yes, indeed! We are capable of proportioning (even) his fingertips."
  75,5,"Still, human being wants to deny what lies before him."
  75,6,He asks: ‘When is the Day of Resurrection?’
  75,7,"So when the eyes are dazzled,"
  75,8,"and the moon will be eclipsed,"
  75,9,"and the sun and the moon are brought together,"
  75,10,"on that Day, humans will say: ‘Where is the escape?’"
  75,11,"No, indeed! There shall be no refuge."
  75,12,"On that Day, the (final) abode will be towards your Lord."
  75,13,"On that Day, human being will be informed about (the deeds) that he has sent forth and left behind."
  75,14,"Rather, human being shall be a clear witness against himself,"
  75,15,though he should offer his excuses.
  75,16,Do not rush your tongue with (the recitation of) this (Qur’an) to hasten (in memorising) it.
  75,17,"Indeed, it is upon Us to collect it (in your breast) and to recite it (by your tongue)."
  75,18,"So once We have recited it (entirely through Gabriel), follow its recitation."
  75,19,Then its clear explanation is (also) upon Us.
